<hr data-start="86" data-end="89">
<div class="group relative clear-both my-4 w-full overflow-visible"><div id="writing-block-a3718e02-5c03-4993-9c94-2e8ee2fdd419" class="relative w-full overflow-clip rounded-[24px] bg-token-bg-primary dark:bg-[#2a2a2a] shadow-[0px_4px_80px_rgba(0,0,0,0.02)]" data-writing-block="true" data-testid="writing-block-container"><div class="z-1 md:sticky top-(--sticky-padding-top)" data-testid="writing-block-header-sticky-container"><div class="bg-token-bg-primary flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-3 font-sans dark:bg-[#2a2a2a] py-2.5" data-testid="writing-block-header-surface" style="padding-left: calc(5 * var(--spacing)); padding-right: calc(1 * var(--spacing));"><div class="flex grow gap-3 items-center"><div class="text-token-text-tertiary flex max-w-[75%] min-w-0 grow cursor-default items-center self-center text-sm font-medium"><div class="truncate">Writing</div></div></div><div class="flex shrink-0 items-center"><div class="flex items-center"><button class="gap-1 select-none text-sm font-medium text-token-text-primary hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary flex size-9 items-center justify-center rounded-full p-1.5 transition-colors disabled:opacity-40 disabled:hover:bg-transparent" aria-label="Copy" data-state="closed"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-md"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-00d8790d.svg#ce3544" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button></div></div></div></div><div class="writing-block-editor markdown-new-styling relative flow-root pt-(--writing-block-editor-pt) pe-(--writing-block-editor-pr) pb-(--writing-block-editor-pb) ps-(--writing-block-editor-pl)" style="--writing-block-editor-pt: 0px; --writing-block-editor-pr: calc(5 * var(--spacing)); --writing-block-editor-pb: calc(4 * var(--spacing)); --writing-block-editor-pl: calc(5 * var(--spacing));"><div class="ProseMirror markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full min-h-6 break-words focus:outline-none" contenteditable="true" aria-disabled="false" dir="auto" translate="no"><h1><strong><span>DATA SCIENCE INTERNSHIP REPORT</span></strong></h1><h2><strong><span>Task-02: Data Cleaning and Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)</span></strong></h2><h3><strong><span>Internship at Prodigy Infotech</span></strong></h3><div contenteditable="false"><hr></div><h2><strong><span>1. Introduction</span></strong></h2><p><span>This report presents the work completed as part of Task-02 during my Data Science Internship at Prodigy Infotech. The objective of this task is to perform </span><strong><span>data cleaning</span></strong><span> and </span><strong><span>exploratory data analysis (EDA)</span></strong><span> on a dataset to identify patterns, relationships, and trends.</span></p><p><span>For this task, the </span><strong><span>Titanic dataset</span></strong><span> was used, which contains information about passengers such as age, gender, ticket class, and fare.</span></p><div contenteditable="false"><hr></div><h2><strong><span>2. Objective</span></strong></h2><p><span>The main objectives of this task are:</span></p><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>To clean the dataset by handling missing or inconsistent data</span></p></li><li><p><span>To explore the dataset using statistical and visualization techniques</span></p></li><li><p><span>To identify patterns and relationships between variables</span></p></li><li><p><span>To draw meaningful insights from the data</span></p></li></ul><div contenteditable="false"><hr></div><h2><strong><span>3. Dataset Description</span></strong></h2><p><span>The dataset used is the Titanic dataset, which includes the following key features:</span></p><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><strong><span>PassengerId</span></strong><span> – Unique ID of each passenger</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span>Pclass</span></strong><span> – Passenger class (1st, 2nd, 3rd)</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span>Name</span></strong><span> – Passenger name</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span>Sex</span></strong><span> – Gender</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span>Age</span></strong><span> – Age of passenger</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span>SibSp</span></strong><span> – Number of siblings/spouses aboard</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span>Parch</span></strong><span> – Number of parents/children aboard</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span>Ticket</span></strong><span> – Ticket number</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span>Fare</span></strong><span> – Ticket fare</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span>Cabin</span></strong><span> – Cabin number</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span>Embarked</span></strong><span> – Port of embarkation</span></p></li></ul><div contenteditable="false"><hr></div><h2><strong><span>4. Data Cleaning</span></strong></h2><p><span>Data cleaning is an essential step to ensure accuracy and reliability of analysis.</span></p><h3><strong><span>Steps Performed:</span></strong></h3><ol data-spread="true" start="1"><li><p><strong><span>Handling Missing Values:</span></strong></p><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>The </span><code dir="ltr"><span>Age</span></code><span> column contained missing values, which were filled using the </span><strong><span>median</span></strong><span>.</span></p></li><li><p><span>The </span><code dir="ltr"><span>Fare</span></code><span> column had missing values, which were also filled using the </span><strong><span>median</span></strong><span>.</span></p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong><span>Dropping Irrelevant Columns:</span></strong></p><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>The </span><code dir="ltr"><span>Cabin</span></code><span> column contained a large number of missing values and was removed.</span></p></li></ul></li><li><p><strong><span>Verification:</span></strong></p><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>After cleaning, the dataset was checked again to confirm that no missing values remained.</span></p></li></ul></li></ol><div contenteditable="false"><hr></div><h2><strong><span>5. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)</span></strong></h2><p><span>EDA was performed using visualization libraries such as Matplotlib and Seaborn.</span></p><h3><strong><span>5.1 Gender Distribution</span></strong></h3><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>A count plot showed that the number of male passengers is higher than female passengers.</span></p></li></ul><h3><strong><span>5.2 Passenger Class Distribution</span></strong></h3><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>Most passengers belong to </span><strong><span>3rd class</span></strong><span>, indicating a majority of lower-income travelers.</span></p></li></ul><h3><strong><span>5.3 Age Distribution</span></strong></h3><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>The majority of passengers are between </span><strong><span>20 and 40 years old</span></strong><span>.</span></p></li></ul><h3><strong><span>5.4 Fare Distribution</span></strong></h3><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>The fare distribution is </span><strong><span>right-skewed</span></strong><span>, meaning most passengers paid lower fares, while a few paid significantly higher fares.</span></p></li></ul><h3><strong><span>5.5 Relationship between Passenger Class and Fare</span></strong></h3><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>A box plot showed that </span><strong><span>1st class passengers paid higher fares</span></strong><span>, followed by 2nd and 3rd class.</span></p></li></ul><h3><strong><span>5.6 Gender vs Passenger Class</span></strong></h3><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>Males are more common across all classes, especially in 3rd class.</span></p></li></ul><h3><strong><span>5.7 Correlation Analysis</span></strong></h3><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>A heatmap was used to analyze relationships between numerical variables.</span></p></li><li><p><span>Weak to moderate correlations were observed among features like fare and class.</span></p></li></ul><div contenteditable="false"><hr></div><h2><strong><span>6. Key Findings</span></strong></h2><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>The dataset is dominated by </span><strong><span>3rd class passengers</span></strong></p></li><li><p><strong><span>Male passengers</span></strong><span> are more than female passengers</span></p></li><li><p><span>Most passengers fall within the </span><strong><span>20–40 age group</span></strong></p></li><li><p><span>Ticket fares vary significantly depending on class</span></p></li><li><p><span>Higher passenger class is associated with higher fares</span></p></li></ul><div contenteditable="false"><hr></div><h2><strong><span>7. Conclusion</span></strong></h2><p><span>This task successfully demonstrated the importance of data cleaning and exploratory data analysis. By handling missing values and visualizing data, meaningful insights were extracted from the dataset.</span></p><p><span>EDA helped in understanding the structure of the dataset and identifying trends, which are essential steps before applying machine learning models.</span></p><div contenteditable="false"><hr></div><h2><strong><span>8. Tools and Technologies Used</span></strong></h2><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>Python</span></p></li><li><p><span>Pandas</span></p></li><li><p><span>Matplotlib</span></p></li><li><p><span>Seaborn</span></p></li><li><p><span>Jupyter Notebook / Google Colab</span></p></li></ul><div contenteditable="false"><hr></div><h2><strong><span>9. Learning Outcomes</span></strong></h2><ul data-spread="false"><li><p><span>Gained practical experience in </span><strong><span>data cleaning techniques</span></strong></p></li><li><p><span>Learned how to perform </span><strong><span>EDA using visualization tools</span></strong></p></li><li><p><span>Improved understanding of </span><strong><span>data patterns and relationships</span></strong></p></li><li><p><span>Developed skills in interpreting and presenting data insights</span></p></li></ul><div contenteditable="false"><hr></div><p><strong><span>Submitted by:</span></strong><br><span><span data-placeholder-token="true" class="text-token-text-primary cursor-text rounded-sm" style="background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--theme-user-selection-bg, var(--selection)) 30%, transparent); padding-top: 4px; padding-bottom: 4px;">[Your Name]</span></span></p><p><strong><span>Internship:</span></strong><span> Data Science Internship</span></p><p><strong><span>Organization:</span></strong><span> Prodigy Infotech</span></p><div contenteditable="false"><hr></div></div></div><div aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 z-2 rounded-[24px] shadow-[inset_0px_0px_0px_1px_rgba(0,0,0,0.07)]"></div></div></div>
