ll wrap-break-word light markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="158">Great — this means your model is working perfectly ✅<br data-start="52" data-end="55">
Now let me <strong data-start="66" data-end="112">explain this decision tree in a simple way</strong> so you can also write it in your viva/report.</p>
<hr data-start="160" data-end="163">
<h1 data-section-id="1hmarkc" data-start="165" data-end="195">🌳 What this Tree Represents</h1>
<p data-start="197" data-end="274">This is a <strong data-start="207" data-end="235">Decision Tree Classifier</strong> built using your <strong data-start="253" data-end="273">bank.csv dataset</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="276" data-end="346">👉 It predicts:<br>
<strong data-start="292" data-end="346">Will a customer subscribe to a product? (Yes / No)</strong></p>
<hr data-start="348" data-end="351">
<h1 data-section-id="1tela4h" data-start="353" data-end="379">🧠 How to Read This Tree</h1>
<h2 data-section-id="qxnhkt" data-start="381" data-end="420">🔹 1. Start from the TOP (Root Node)</h2>
<ul data-start="421" data-end="517">
<li data-section-id="1ktofra" data-start="421" data-end="460">
<p data-start="423" data-end="460">The top box is the <strong data-start="442" data-end="460">first decision</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1r6txa2" data-start="461" data-end="517">
<p data-start="463" data-end="517">It splits data based on the <strong data-start="491" data-end="517">most important feature</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="519" data-end="553">Example idea:<br>
👉 <code data-start="536" data-end="553">duration &lt;= 200</code></p>
<p data-start="555" data-end="566">This means:</p>
<ul data-start="567" data-end="612">
<li data-section-id="120nbyo" data-start="567" data-end="588">
<p data-start="569" data-end="588">If TRUE → go left</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1rfbiyo" data-start="589" data-end="612">
<p data-start="591" data-end="612">If FALSE → go right</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="614" data-end="617">
<h2 data-section-id="16lh3rp" data-start="619" data-end="649">🔹 2. Each Box = A Question</h2>
<p data-start="651" data-end="701">Every node asks:<br>
👉 “Does this condition satisfy?”</p>
<p data-start="703" data-end="711">Example:</p>
<ul data-start="712" data-end="745">
<li data-section-id="1nf9fu6" data-start="712" data-end="731">
<p data-start="714" data-end="731"><code data-start="714" data-end="731">balance &lt;= 1000</code></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="iye2p8" data-start="732" data-end="745">
<p data-start="734" data-end="745"><code data-start="734" data-end="745">age &lt;= 35</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="747" data-end="750">
<h2 data-section-id="1yk1hts" data-start="752" data-end="781">🔹 3. Branches = Decisions</h2>
<p data-start="783" data-end="812">Each split creates two paths:</p>
<ul data-start="813" data-end="864">
<li data-section-id="1cetmzn" data-start="813" data-end="837">
<p data-start="815" data-end="837"><strong data-start="815" data-end="837">Left branch → True</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1trrptf" data-start="838" data-end="864">
<p data-start="840" data-end="864"><strong data-start="840" data-end="864">Right branch → False</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="866" data-end="869">
<h2 data-section-id="siomej" data-start="871" data-end="902">🔹 4. Leaf Nodes (End Boxes)</h2>
<p data-start="904" data-end="978">At the bottom, you see final boxes:<br>
👉 These give the <strong data-start="958" data-end="978">final prediction</strong></p>
<p data-start="980" data-end="988">Usually:</p>
<ul data-start="989" data-end="1041">
<li data-section-id="1ccsnco" data-start="989" data-end="1027">
<p data-start="991" data-end="1027">Blue → YES (customer will subscribe)</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1kqcb8r" data-start="1028" data-end="1041">
<p data-start="1030" data-end="1041">Orange → NO</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1043" data-end="1046">
<h1 data-section-id="1vwnzsr" data-start="1048" data-end="1082">🔍 Why Your Tree Looks So BIG 😅</h1>
<p data-start="1084" data-end="1110">👉 This is normal because:</p>
<ul data-start="1111" data-end="1173">
<li data-section-id="17wsaqk" data-start="1111" data-end="1142">
<p data-start="1113" data-end="1142">Dataset has <strong data-start="1125" data-end="1142">many features</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1bq8a7r" data-start="1143" data-end="1173">
<p data-start="1145" data-end="1173">No restriction on tree depth</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-section-id="fhrfh4" data-start="1175" data-end="1190">⚠️ Problem:</h3>
<p data-start="1191" data-end="1221">This is called <strong data-start="1206" data-end="1221">Overfitting</strong></p>
<p data-start="1223" data-end="1231">Meaning:</p>
<ul data-start="1232" data-end="1283">
<li data-section-id="g2g370" data-start="1232" data-end="1283">
<p data-start="1234" data-end="1283">Model memorizes data instead of learning patterns</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1285" data-end="1288">
<h1 data-section-id="1xu54pa" data-start="1290" data-end="1334">💡 Key Observations (IMPORTANT for report)</h1>
<p data-start="1336" data-end="1348">You can say:</p>
<ul data-start="1350" data-end="1647">
<li data-section-id="17t7quy" data-start="1350" data-end="1435">
<p data-start="1352" data-end="1435">The tree uses multiple features like <strong data-start="1389" data-end="1415">duration, age, balance</strong> to make decisions</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="ylt30y" data-start="1436" data-end="1509">
<p data-start="1438" data-end="1509">Most splits happen on <strong data-start="1460" data-end="1483">important variables</strong> (especially <code data-start="1496" data-end="1506">duration</code>)</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="1tkmhza" data-start="1510" data-end="1584">
<p data-start="1512" data-end="1584">The tree is <strong data-start="1524" data-end="1549">very deep and complex</strong>, indicating possible overfitting</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id="x85y1a" data-start="1585" data-end="1647">
<p data-start="1587" data-end="1647">Some branches are small → meaning less important decisions</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1649" data-end="1652">
<h1 data-section-id="1r3otqo" data-start="1654" data-end="1699">🚀 How to Make It Better (VERY IMPORTANT ⭐)</h1>
<p data-start="1701" data-end="1725">Use this improved model:</p>
<pre class="overflow-visible! px-0!" data-start="1727" data-end="1812"><div class="relative w-full mt-4 mb-1"><div class=""><div class="relative"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0"><div class="h-full min-h-0 min-w-0" style="width: 100%; transform: none;"><div class="border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl"><div class="h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl lxnfua_clipPathFallback"><div class="sticky z-2 select-none top-(--sticky-padding-top)"><div class="flex w-full items-center justify-between py-1.5 ps-4 pe-1.5 font-sans md:ps-5 bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary"><div class="flex max-w-[75%] min-w-0 cursor-default items-center text-sm font-medium justify-self-start text-token-text-primary"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-sm me-2.5 shrink-0"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-00d8790d.svg#e45ab3" fill="currentColor"></use></svg>Python</div><div class="flex flex-row items-center gap-0.5 justify-self-end"><button class="flex gap-1 items-center select-none py-2 text-sm font-medium hover:bg-black/5 dark:hover:bg-white/10 size-9 rounded-full px-2" aria-label="Copy" data-state="closed"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-md"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-00d8790d.svg#ce3544" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></button><button class="btn relative group-focus-within/dialog:focus-visible:[outline-width:1.5px] group-focus-within/dialog:focus-visible:[outline-offset:2.5px] group-focus-within/dialog:focus-visible:[outline-style:solid] group-focus-within/dialog:focus-visible:[outline-color:var(--text-primary)] btn-ghost border-token-border-default ms-2 border font-sans" aria-label="Run code" type="button"><div class="flex w-full items-center justify-center gap-1.5"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-label="